      "text": "Economic history sits at the intersection of economics (models, quantification) and history (context, narrative, contingency). The field answers questions that neither discipline can answer alone: *Why did sustained growth begin when and where it did? What caused the Great Divergence? How do institutions shape long-run outcomes?*"
